        "original_id": "bbc400dc-9c41-5a54-a892-2c126fdfbb60",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: The Highwaymen\n- People: Johnny Cash, Waylon Jennings, Willie Nelson, Kris Kristofferson, Jimmy Webb\n- Products: “Highwayman”\n- Concepts: outlaw country, reincarnation across time\n\nFacts:\n- Jimmy Webb wrote the song “Highwayman.”\n- “Highwayman” is about one soul incarnated in four different times and roles: a highwayman, a sailor, a Hoover Dam construction worker, and a starship captain.\n- The Highwaymen was a country music supergroup.\n- The Highwaymen consisted of Johnny Cash, Waylon Jennings, Willie Nelson, and Kris Kristofferson.\n- The four members of The Highwaymen were major country artists known for pioneering influence on the outlaw country subgenre.",
